  "question": {
    "text": "A transmitting antenna is kept on the surface of the earth. The minimum height of receiving antenna required to receive the signal in line of sight at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math> distance from it is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _____.<br />(Let, radius of earth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi></math>)",
    "image": null
